    "updated_at": "2026-06-30T06:56:09Z",
    "body": "  I tried this on latest image and I think the issue may not be caused by reading prefix-cache hits.\n\n  On current `main`, `prompt_logprobs=0` should already skip prefix-cache reads request-wise:\n\n  - `SamplingParams` sets `skip_reading_prefix_cache = self.prompt_logprobs is not None`, so `prompt_logprobs=0` is included:\n    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/fb42e5219/vllm/sampling_params.py#L500-L504\n  - `Request` propagates the flag:\n    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/fb42e5219/vllm/v1/request.py#L266-L277\n  - `KVCacheManager.get_computed_blocks()` returns no cached blocks when the flag is set:\n    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/fb42e5219/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_manager.py#L214-L219\n\n  I also reran the repro with `vllm/vllm-openai:latest-ubuntu2404` (`vllm 0.24.0`, `torch 2.11.0+cu130`, H200). I still see order-sensitive prompt-logprob\n  diffs, but the results are essentially the same with prefix caching on and off:\n\n  ```text\n  enable_prefix_caching=True:\n    shuffled prompt 1 max diff = 0.040478230\n    shuffled prompt 3 max diff = 0.005993247\n\n  enable_prefix_caching=False:\n    shuffled prompt 1 max diff = 0.040478230\n    shuffled prompt 3 max diff = 0.005993247\n\n  I also ran the original script shape with only enable_prefix_caching=False added, and it still produced nonzero diffs.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
